WEBVTT

01:42.644 --> 01:45.522
<i>At first,
we couldn't believe what we were seeing.</i>

01:46.022 --> 01:48.775
<i>We never imagined
that such a thing was even possible.</i>

01:49.692 --> 01:52.654
<i>The first to notice, of course, was Baki.</i>

01:54.405 --> 01:55.323
Huh?

01:55.406 --> 01:57.075
<i>Wounds.</i>

01:57.158 --> 02:00.620
<i>The sort of wounds that might have come
from the slash of a falchion.</i>

02:01.204 --> 02:05.834
<i>The old scars ran in a diagonal line
clear across Pickle's upper body.</i>

02:06.918 --> 02:08.711
<i>Where did those come from?</i>

02:09.629 --> 02:11.756
<i>Looks like he was shot with a machine gun.</i>

02:12.549 --> 02:14.300
<i>He certainly didn't get those here.</i>

02:14.801 --> 02:15.844
<i>Claws?</i>

02:15.927 --> 02:16.970
<i>Spikes?</i>

02:17.887 --> 02:19.973
<i>Must've been something from his own time.</i>

02:20.056 --> 02:22.600
<i>Who or what made them?</i>

02:22.684 --> 02:25.103
<i>What sort of creature
could have inflicted them?</i>

02:25.854 --> 02:28.481
<i>We were about to find out
the amazing answer.</i>

02:29.816 --> 02:33.611
<i>We were stunned when we saw
the same scars ran across his back.</i>

02:35.029 --> 02:36.114
<i>Then we knew.</i>

02:36.698 --> 02:39.450
<i>Matching scars on his front and back.</i>

02:40.034 --> 02:42.245
<i>There is only one thing it could mean.</i>

02:42.787 --> 02:46.082
<i>From their shape, their size, their age...</i>

02:47.458 --> 02:50.503
<i>They hadn't been made by a knife,
but by teeth.</i>

02:52.046 --> 02:56.634
<i>Pickle was a man who had survived
the jaws of a Tyrannosaurus Rex!</i>

02:57.218 --> 03:00.305
<i>Our shock, our pity, our esteem,</i>

03:00.930 --> 03:03.099
<i>how do you suppose we expressed them?</i>

03:04.601 --> 03:07.562
<i>As one, without consulting each other,</i>

03:07.645 --> 03:10.732
<i>we all simultaneously began to applaud.</i>

03:16.905 --> 03:21.659
<i>By rearranging his joints,
he transformed into full battle mode.</i>

03:23.244 --> 03:25.914
<i>This was Pickle's final form.</i>

03:25.997 --> 03:27.498
All right.

03:27.582 --> 03:30.168
So now we can really get down to business.

03:30.752 --> 03:33.171
This is when
the real battle begins, right?

03:34.505 --> 03:36.216
<i>His final form,</i>

03:36.299 --> 03:39.219
<i>after he'd adjusted
the joints at his shoulders,</i>

03:39.302 --> 03:41.763
<i>elbows, wrists, and hips,</i>

03:42.388 --> 03:44.182
<i>was truly uncanny.</i>

03:45.058 --> 03:47.435
<i>With the awakening
of his primeval memories,</i>

03:47.518 --> 03:51.022
<i>the densest parts of his body
became even more solid.</i>

03:51.522 --> 03:54.442
<i>The parts that were strong
became even stronger.</i>

03:55.109 --> 03:58.738
<i>The parts that were tough before
became even more resilient.</i>

04:01.157 --> 04:02.450
I'm touched, Pickle.

04:03.034 --> 04:07.121
I'll just take your transformation
as a sign of respect.

04:07.747 --> 04:09.040
A gesture of friendship.

04:09.540 --> 04:10.583
Huh?

04:10.667 --> 04:13.253
<i>Humanity has been
ceaselessly evolving</i>

04:13.336 --> 04:15.213
<i>since the beginning of history.</i>

04:15.296 --> 04:19.676
<i>And over the course of that evolution,
we've acquired many different weapons.</i>

04:20.385 --> 04:25.390
<i>We've used stones,
clubs, swords, guns, missiles,</i>

04:26.182 --> 04:27.725
<i>even nuclear weapons.</i>

04:28.309 --> 04:30.645
<i>But in the process, we've lost something.</i>

04:31.187 --> 04:32.897
<i>We've left something behind.</i>

04:33.690 --> 04:36.567
<i>This is what
this primordial man has taught us.</i>

04:37.944 --> 04:41.823
<i>We've lost the tough skin
and strong bones and muscles,</i>

04:42.699 --> 04:45.243
<i>the fighting spirit
that doesn't succumb to pain.</i>

04:45.827 --> 04:48.871
<i>As we've come to rely
on ever more powerful weapons,</i>

04:48.955 --> 04:52.667
<i>we've lost these other things, one by one,</i>

04:52.750 --> 04:56.212
<i>until we're no longer even capable
of defending ourselves.</i>

04:59.590 --> 05:01.009
<i>I'm right here,</i>

05:01.092 --> 05:02.635
<i>within your range.</i>

05:03.219 --> 05:04.512
<i>I'm not going anywhere.</i>

05:04.595 --> 05:07.890
<i>By standing here right in front of you,</i>

05:08.725 --> 05:10.768
<i>I will return your friendship!</i>

05:13.354 --> 05:16.024
<i>Damn it, Baki. Gotta do better.</i>

05:26.242 --> 05:29.162
<i>Baki should've been sent flying
by Pickle's blow,</i>

05:29.245 --> 05:30.747
<i>but he's barely budged!</i>

05:33.750 --> 05:36.085
I bet I know what you're thinking.

05:36.169 --> 05:38.880
How am I still here after that punch?

05:38.963 --> 05:40.048
It's simple.

05:40.631 --> 05:43.134
I met your strength
with all of my strength,

05:43.760 --> 05:46.471
only quicker and at a sharper angle.

05:47.263 --> 05:50.183
They call it skill. Along with evolution.

05:50.892 --> 05:53.144
You see, we've learned
a few things since your time.

05:53.227 --> 05:54.687
Things like the martial arts!

05:55.938 --> 05:59.442
I'll put what I've got
against what you've got any day!

05:59.525 --> 06:01.694
We match up well in a lot of things.

06:02.362 --> 06:05.823
Strength, speed, stamina, experience.

06:05.907 --> 06:08.201
We're pretty much even on those.

06:08.910 --> 06:12.997
We both know what this means,
and neither of us wants to lose.

06:14.791 --> 06:18.586
But maybe you have the advantage
all the way ‘round.

06:19.128 --> 06:21.964
And of course, when it comes to
the sheer weight and size of our bodies,

06:22.048 --> 06:23.716
there's no comparison.

06:25.301 --> 06:28.596
<i>So, if that's the case,
how can even I fight you?</i>

06:29.180 --> 06:30.848
<i>What do I have to work with?</i>

06:30.932 --> 06:32.225
<i>My moves!</i>

06:32.850 --> 06:35.520
<i>The moves and skills
I've been developing for so long,</i>

06:35.603 --> 06:37.480
<i>I can't even remember when I started.</i>

06:37.563 --> 06:39.107
<i>I've endured pain,</i>

06:39.190 --> 06:40.733
<i>honed my body,</i>

06:40.817 --> 06:42.068
<i>nourished myself,</i>

06:42.151 --> 06:43.986
<i>faced challenges, and fought.</i>

06:44.070 --> 06:46.989
<i>The unconscious formation of the fist.</i>

06:47.073 --> 06:48.991
<i>The instinctive placement of the feet.</i>

06:49.575 --> 06:51.327
<i>The natural breathing rhythm.</i>

06:51.828 --> 06:54.205
<i>Eyes that know exactly what to look for.</i>

06:54.705 --> 06:58.418
<i>These fighting skills
passed down from ancient times</i>

06:58.501 --> 07:00.461
<i>live within me and support me.</i>

07:01.212 --> 07:04.132
<i>Skills that were created
to ensure survival,</i>

07:04.215 --> 07:06.384
<i>sharpened for self-defense,</i>

07:06.467 --> 07:08.094
<i>fed on hatred,</i>

07:08.970 --> 07:10.972
<i>and passed down through sorrow.</i>

07:11.055 --> 07:14.392
<i>These are the links
in the chain that bind me together.</i>

07:16.269 --> 07:18.020
<i>Suddenly, Baki saw it.</i>

07:18.771 --> 07:20.815
<i>Awakened to his own history,</i>

07:20.898 --> 07:23.734
<i>he was now able
to see Pickle's history as well.</i>

07:24.444 --> 07:25.945
<i>It was the same with him!</i>

07:26.612 --> 07:30.741
<i>All those teeth, claws, and horns
from the distant past,</i>

07:30.825 --> 07:34.537
<i>they were what supported him
and made him what he is now.</i>

07:34.620 --> 07:36.747
I guess that makes sense.

07:36.831 --> 07:38.541
You've got your--

07:38.624 --> 07:41.794
<i>Then,
amidst those monstrous weapons,</i>

07:41.878 --> 07:44.005
<i>human figures began to appear.</i>

07:44.088 --> 07:45.965
<i>Oh, now I get it!</i>

07:46.048 --> 07:48.301
<i>Pushing aside the claws
was Retsu.</i>

07:48.384 --> 07:50.928
<i>Standing in front of the teeth
was Katsumi.</i>

07:51.012 --> 07:53.264
<i>Deflecting the horns was Jack.</i>

07:54.765 --> 07:57.018
<i>They, too, had supported Pickle.</i>

07:57.518 --> 08:00.271
What is it? What is it he's seeing?

08:00.771 --> 08:03.691
What's wrong with Pickle? Why's he crying?

08:03.774 --> 08:05.693
This is more than a fight.

08:06.194 --> 08:07.403
It's all-out war.

08:08.029 --> 08:10.490
I've never faced
a more formidable opponent.

08:11.491 --> 08:14.410
<i>What do I do in this situation?
What's my move?</i>

08:15.411 --> 08:17.371
<i>Should I try it?</i>

08:17.455 --> 08:20.208
<i>Just try throwing it out there
and see what happens?</i>

08:20.291 --> 08:22.043
<i>Or do I play it safe?</i>

08:23.169 --> 08:25.213
<i>I could probably dodge or block it.</i>

08:25.296 --> 08:26.714
<i>Man, what should I do?</i>

08:26.797 --> 08:29.675
<i>You're running out of time.
You gotta make a decision.</i>

08:33.930 --> 08:36.098
<i>Oh, so that's what it is, huh?</i>

08:36.682 --> 08:38.476
<i>Bold choice!</i>

08:40.061 --> 08:41.771
<i>You didn't dodge or block.</i>

08:41.854 --> 08:44.065
<i>You literally beat him to the punch.</i>

08:45.775 --> 08:48.694
<i>You have to anticipate
your opponent's moves,</i>

08:49.320 --> 08:50.821
<i>get into his flow,</i>

08:50.905 --> 08:53.491
<i>and use his own momentum to counterattack.</i>

08:57.828 --> 09:01.249
<i>Now, you'll get two effects
from a solid counter-punch.</i>

09:01.332 --> 09:03.709
<i>There's the physical effect, of course.</i>

09:03.793 --> 09:07.255
<i>Even a small amount of force
can have an outsized impact.</i>

09:07.838 --> 09:12.843
<i>But even more important is
its effect on your opponent's morale.</i>

09:14.303 --> 09:17.431
<i>When your heart and mind
are solely focused on attacking,</i>

09:17.515 --> 09:21.143
<i>your jaw tends to fall open,
your neck muscles go slack.</i>

09:22.353 --> 09:25.773
<i>At that moment,
you've forgotten that you can get hit too.</i>

09:25.856 --> 09:30.111
<i>You don't easily recover from a blow
like that before the count of ten.</i>

09:30.611 --> 09:33.990
<i>When a fighter, any fighter,
forgets that he can be hit,</i>

09:34.073 --> 09:36.409
<i>even as strong
and tough a fighter as Pickle,</i>

09:36.993 --> 09:40.538
<i>he becomes as defenseless
as a newborn infant.</i>

09:42.164 --> 09:45.334
<i>There was once a boxer
with a punch so devastating</i>

09:45.418 --> 09:48.504
<i>that it was said he could
stop an elephant in its tracks.</i>

09:48.588 --> 09:52.049
<i>That man was George Foreman,
the heavyweight champion of the world,</i>

09:52.633 --> 09:55.094
<i>and he had the highest knockout rate
in history,</i>

09:55.177 --> 09:58.723
<i>though the great majority of his victories
had come from technical knockouts</i>

09:58.806 --> 10:00.308
<i>and not ten-counts.</i>

10:00.391 --> 10:02.893
<i>Facing him was a fighter
who'd been described</i>

10:02.977 --> 10:06.480
<i>as, pound-for-pound,
the weakest champion in history,</i>

10:06.564 --> 10:09.317
<i>Muhammad Ali, known as "The Greatest."</i>

10:09.984 --> 10:12.236
<i>With his lightning-fast "phantom punches,"</i>

10:12.320 --> 10:14.905
<i>he forced many boxers, including Foreman,</i>

10:14.989 --> 10:17.450
<i>to endure the losing end of a ten-count.</i>

10:18.659 --> 10:21.287
<i>A clever counter-punch
comes out of nowhere.</i>

10:22.246 --> 10:24.498
<i>A complete surprise to the opponent.</i>

10:25.082 --> 10:27.126
<i>That's exactly what Baki did.</i>

10:27.918 --> 10:32.089
<i>That's how he was able to trade punches
with a larger and stronger man.</i>

10:32.173 --> 10:34.842
<i>That's how he forced Pickle
back against the ropes.</i>

10:34.925 --> 10:38.596
<i>"I've been attacked
by giant teeth," Pickle told himself.</i>

10:38.679 --> 10:40.973
<i>"“But I smashed them all with my fists."</i>

10:41.682 --> 10:44.435
<i>"I've been attacked by razor-sharp claws,</i>

10:44.518 --> 10:47.229
<i>but I grabbed them,
twisted and broke them."</i>

10:48.230 --> 10:51.484
<i>"Whenever I was attacked,
this is what I did."</i>

10:51.567 --> 10:54.487
<i>"Against great size, I won."</i>

10:54.570 --> 10:57.365
<i>"Against great speed, I won."</i>

10:57.448 --> 10:58.991
<i>"I won."</i>

10:59.075 --> 11:00.618
<i>"I won."</i>

11:01.369 --> 11:02.370
<i>"I won."</i>

11:03.496 --> 11:05.623
<i>"In my world, I was the greatest."</i>

11:07.208 --> 11:09.502
<i>"But in this world, I feel cornered."</i>

11:11.962 --> 11:14.507
He's cornered Pickle!

11:14.590 --> 11:18.511
<i>His size advantage
wasn't working.</i>

11:18.594 --> 11:22.264
<i>His strength advantage wasn't working.</i>

11:23.224 --> 11:25.601
<i>The primordial man was bewildered.</i>

11:25.685 --> 11:28.020
He had never encountered moves like this,

11:28.688 --> 11:31.232
<i>or such mystifying fighting skills.</i>

11:31.315 --> 11:32.274
<i>And then...</i>

11:34.360 --> 11:35.778
Huh? What?

11:37.363 --> 11:39.031
I can't even see him!

11:39.115 --> 11:43.285
Like in his fight with Jack,
it's lightning-fast teleportation.

11:43.369 --> 11:46.205
<i>Pickle is trying to take cover.</i>

11:46.288 --> 11:47.456
<i>But it's not working.</i>

11:47.540 --> 11:50.835
<i>Everywhere he goes,
Baki's right there with him!</i>

11:54.255 --> 11:56.757
I told you, you remember?

11:57.800 --> 12:01.303
<i>I'm staying right here.
I'm not going anywhere.</i>

12:02.972 --> 12:05.057
<i>The huge difference in size,</i>

12:05.141 --> 12:07.435
<i>the vast disparity in strength,</i>

12:07.518 --> 12:12.064
<i>they were overcome by a tool
of civilization known as the martial arts.</i>

12:12.773 --> 12:15.067
<i>Baki was on the verge of victory.</i>

12:17.903 --> 12:19.447
<i>At that moment,</i>

12:19.530 --> 12:22.032
<i>as glory fell within his reach,</i>

12:22.116 --> 12:24.827
<i>something new sprouted
in the young man's heart.</i>

12:26.370 --> 12:28.330
<i>A bad habit was born.</i>

12:29.415 --> 12:32.376
<i>As he gazed
at the other's out-thrust fists,</i>

12:32.460 --> 12:34.712
<i>it dawned on Pickle
that this man was offering him</i>

12:34.795 --> 12:38.674
<i>the opportunity to decide this fight
on stamina alone.</i>

12:41.927 --> 12:44.472
<i>It was a reckless act
of insatiable greed</i>

12:44.555 --> 12:45.723
<i>on the young man's part.</i>

12:45.806 --> 12:49.685
<i>He had carelessly thrown away
a sure victory earned by his skills,</i>

12:49.769 --> 12:51.479
<i>and instead sought to prove</i>

12:51.562 --> 12:54.732
<i>that he could beat his opponent
in a test of stamina.</i>

12:54.815 --> 12:58.861
<i>It wasn't long before the difference
in their stamina was manifested,</i>

12:58.944 --> 13:02.823
<i>and the result was as inevitable
as the sun rising in the east</i>

13:02.907 --> 13:05.451
<i>or water flowing to the lowest point.</i>

13:08.954 --> 13:10.873
<i>Pickle executed a move!</i>

13:11.832 --> 13:15.753
<i>During the course of this contest,
he had sensed his own fear,</i>

13:15.836 --> 13:18.214
<i>the fear of losing to this modern man.</i>

13:18.839 --> 13:20.633
<i>And motivated by this fear...</i>

13:22.218 --> 13:25.179
<i>...the primordial man
had acquired a new weapon.</i>

13:26.096 --> 13:27.848
<i>Their battle was over.</i>

13:39.193 --> 13:41.320
Hmm.

13:42.112 --> 13:44.281
Pickle's not even trying to move.

13:44.365 --> 13:46.951
And Baki couldn't move if he tried.

13:47.034 --> 13:47.952
Well, then,

13:48.035 --> 13:50.579
do either of you two have an opinion?

13:50.663 --> 13:51.956
Foolish question.

13:53.415 --> 13:55.960
There's only one opinion
that anyone could have.

13:56.627 --> 14:00.965
If Pickle had wanted to kill Baki,
he certainly could have.

14:01.715 --> 14:03.968
So clearly, Pickle won.

14:04.051 --> 14:05.010
Huh.

14:06.637 --> 14:08.973
I have a different opinion.

14:09.557 --> 14:10.474
Oh?

14:11.058 --> 14:15.563
The only way the weak
can ever compete against the strong

14:16.355 --> 14:18.440
Is by executing moves.

14:19.233 --> 14:20.985
Moves are weapons.

14:21.068 --> 14:22.528
Uh-huh...

14:22.611 --> 14:25.573
Pickle is strong already.
And huge.

14:27.032 --> 14:29.785
For him to have acquired
that weapon as well...

14:34.832 --> 14:36.250
It's an unwritten rule

14:36.333 --> 14:40.629
that the strong don't have
the right to use tricks.

14:41.463 --> 14:44.466
That's funny coming from you,
Kaoru Hanayama.

14:44.550 --> 14:47.386
You were born with strength to spare.

14:47.469 --> 14:49.179
What do you say about Baki?

14:49.263 --> 14:52.141
Pretty sure we just watched him
back Pickle into a corner!

14:52.224 --> 14:56.395
My heart tells me
the victory should be his.

14:56.979 --> 14:59.273
<i>Retsu,
who lives by martial arts,</i>

14:59.356 --> 15:01.984
<i>and Hanayama, who lives by masculinity,</i>

15:02.067 --> 15:04.403
<i>you are both right and you are both harsh.</i>

15:10.743 --> 15:13.662
- Look!
- He's standing! How?

15:27.885 --> 15:30.763
We're going to let him just walk out?

15:31.263 --> 15:33.140
Oh, let him go.

15:33.223 --> 15:35.059
He's not an animal, after all.

15:35.142 --> 15:38.896
Though Professor Payne
will probably throw a fit.

15:40.898 --> 15:44.276
Well, it seems
my patient has walked out on me.

15:44.777 --> 15:48.030
Obviously, my services weren't needed.

15:48.113 --> 15:48.948
Waste of time.

15:52.576 --> 15:55.162
<i>Whenever he's hurt
and feeling depressed,</i>

15:55.871 --> 15:58.207
<i>there's a sight he longs to see.</i>

15:59.541 --> 16:00.501
Good choice.

16:01.085 --> 16:03.212
This spot definitely has the best view.

16:08.300 --> 16:10.886
It's amazing how much
you can see from up here.

16:11.470 --> 16:12.972
And how far too.

16:14.306 --> 16:17.059
All the way back to a time before history,

16:17.559 --> 16:18.978
when none of this was here.

16:19.728 --> 16:21.772
When the world was new and untouched.

16:22.773 --> 16:24.024
When it was your world.

16:25.567 --> 16:26.735
It's beautiful.

16:29.405 --> 16:33.075
Mind if I... sit here and share it with you?

16:40.791 --> 16:43.627
<i>On that same day,
in Washington, D.C.,</i>

16:43.711 --> 16:47.881
<i>a secret meeting was taking place
at the prestigious St. Renas Hotel.</i>

16:48.465 --> 16:51.760
<i>Prior to this meeting,
a 700-meter security perimeter</i>

16:51.844 --> 16:54.388
<i>had been established around the location.</i>

16:56.140 --> 16:58.267
In all this time
since I've been in office,

16:58.350 --> 17:00.644
this must be the first time
I've taken a meeting

17:00.728 --> 17:04.106
without, uh, having the Secret Service
hiding in the woodwork.

17:04.189 --> 17:06.608
Which, when you think about it,
is a little bit strange,

17:06.692 --> 17:08.402
since you're generally considered

17:08.485 --> 17:10.904
one of the most dangerous people
on the planet.

17:13.323 --> 17:14.992
You sure talk a lot.

17:15.075 --> 17:16.535
Oh. Sorry.

17:16.618 --> 17:19.329
Well, allow me to, uh,
get straight to the point, then.

17:19.413 --> 17:22.583
Ever since the time
of my predecessor, Ronald Reegan,

17:22.666 --> 17:26.628
every single U.S. president has signed
a formal Treaty of Friendship

17:26.712 --> 17:30.382
with the man known as "the Ogre,"
or Yujiro Hanma.

17:31.216 --> 17:33.969
I was only informed of this secret
just last week.

17:34.511 --> 17:37.056
- And I must say, when I first--
- Hey!

17:37.139 --> 17:39.266
Just get on with it, will ya?

17:39.349 --> 17:41.560
Sorry. I got carried away.

17:41.643 --> 17:43.103
Okay, let's wrap this up.

17:43.187 --> 17:45.022
I won't waste any more of your time.

17:47.775 --> 17:51.278
I hereby swear
that the United States of America8

17:51.361 --> 17:54.406
will do its utmost
to maintain an amicable relationship

17:54.490 --> 17:55.949
with Master Yujiro Hanma.

17:56.033 --> 17:57.868
That we will respect your interests,

17:57.951 --> 18:00.662
and leave you free
to pursue them as you see fit.

18:00.746 --> 18:03.415
That we will never interfere
with you or your actions,

18:03.499 --> 18:05.709
regardless of anything that might happen.

18:05.793 --> 18:09.797
That I will faithfully execute and abide
by this treaty of friendship,

18:09.880 --> 18:11.465
I do solemnly swear,

18:11.548 --> 18:15.385
as President of the United States,
Barack Ozma.

18:16.512 --> 18:19.723
It's a pain to have
to do this every four years.

18:23.143 --> 18:24.061
Hmm?

18:24.561 --> 18:25.771
A lump of coal.

18:25.854 --> 18:30.109
They say if you apply pressure to it
equal to 100,000 atmospheres,

18:30.192 --> 18:31.944
it will turn into a diamond.

18:32.820 --> 18:37.491
Now, that's not something that most folks
get a chance to see with their own eyes.

18:37.574 --> 18:39.243
So I was thinking, Mr. Ogre,

18:39.785 --> 18:42.955
if it's true you're more powerful
than a nuclear bomb,

18:43.038 --> 18:45.332
maybe you could do it
with your bare hands?

18:46.500 --> 18:47.876
You too, huh?

18:48.502 --> 18:51.046
You're no different than President Bosch.

18:57.719 --> 19:01.974
<i>He cut that glass tabletop in half,
just as if he were using a diamond!</i>

19:05.394 --> 19:07.521
It's not worth as much as a real one.

19:08.814 --> 19:09.898
Oh damn.

19:10.482 --> 19:12.025
Yes, you could!

19:17.656 --> 19:19.408
<i>As for what to do about Pickle,</i>

19:19.491 --> 19:21.660
<i>I don't think there's any room for debate.</i>

19:22.202 --> 19:25.330
<i>The only humane choice is
to return him to his original state.</i>

19:25.956 --> 19:29.501
<i>After all, it's only because
of human curiosity that he's even here.</i>

19:30.002 --> 19:33.005
Professor Payne, what do you think?

19:33.505 --> 19:35.591
You make it sound so simple.

19:36.091 --> 19:38.427
If by "returning him
to his original state,"

19:38.510 --> 19:42.347
you mean we should put him back
in that salt mine on Colorado,

19:42.431 --> 19:46.018
what's to prevent him
from being unearthed again years from now?

19:46.101 --> 19:49.688
Will Pickle fit in any better
in a society in the distant future?

19:49.771 --> 19:52.774
I have to say
that this "humane" solution of yours

19:52.858 --> 19:55.402
doesn't strike me
as much of a solution at all.

19:55.986 --> 19:58.447
You'll merely be kicking our problem
down the road

19:58.530 --> 20:01.325
and leaving it
for a later generation to deal with.

20:01.408 --> 20:02.826
I quite agree.

20:03.368 --> 20:06.705
Pickle is our responsibility,
and <i>we</i> should resolve this situation.

20:07.414 --> 20:09.166
Tell me, Mr. Strydum.

20:09.249 --> 20:13.003
Are they true,
these rumors that we've all heard?

20:13.086 --> 20:15.589
That you've forced
that priceless human artifact

20:15.672 --> 20:17.633
to engage in bloody hand-to hand combat

20:17.716 --> 20:19.968
with various fighters
and martial arts specialists?

20:20.052 --> 20:22.930
<i>I was honoring
the promise I made to him.</i>

20:23.013 --> 20:24.806
<i>Promise?
How can you make a promise</i>

20:24.890 --> 20:27.517
<i>to someone who doesn't
even understand language?</i>

20:27.601 --> 20:30.229
<i>It wasn't
a promise made with words.</i>

20:30.312 --> 20:31.855
<i>In classrooms,</i>

20:31.939 --> 20:33.357
<i>in workplaces,</i>

20:33.941 --> 20:36.526
<i>anywhere and everywhere
that people gathered,</i>

20:36.610 --> 20:39.696
<i>the topic of what to do
with Pickle was discussed.</i>

20:39.780 --> 20:44.368
<i>It was debated in Europe, America,
Asia, and in the United Nations,</i>

20:45.160 --> 20:46.703
<i>until it was finally resolved</i>

20:46.787 --> 20:49.873
<i>to allow the people of the world
to decide his fate.</i>

20:53.001 --> 20:54.753
500,001,572 VOTES

20:57.464 --> 20:58.882
500,000,543 VOTES

20:59.841 --> 21:03.220
<i>After a worldwide referendum
of one billion people,</i>

21:03.887 --> 21:07.391
<i>and by a margin
of little more than 1,000 votes,</i>

21:08.725 --> 21:10.394
<i>a decision was made.</i>

21:11.979 --> 21:14.481
What's your reaction
to the outcome, Professor Payne?

21:14.564 --> 21:15.482
Disappointment.

21:16.024 --> 21:19.653
However, we must abide
by the decision the people have made.

21:19.736 --> 21:22.364
I have no choice but to remain silent.

21:29.371 --> 21:33.792
Those 1,000 votes are proof
that humanity are fools.

21:37.379 --> 21:41.425
<i>This outcome can only be described
as very unfortunate for Pickle.</i>

21:42.634 --> 21:45.304
We're avoiding our responsibility.

21:45.387 --> 21:49.599
We're just sealing away the opportunity
to unlock the riddle of Pickle.

21:54.146 --> 21:56.064
What in the world is this?

21:57.899 --> 22:00.444
- It's... it's Pickle!
- What's he doing here?!

22:01.486 --> 22:04.990
<i>This was Pickle's way
of showing Strydum his appreciation.</i>

22:05.615 --> 22:09.202
<i>He had brought him a gift,
for having fulfilled his promise.</i>

22:14.207 --> 22:19.379
<i>Pickle scoffed at the world,
and vanished into the maze of Tokyo.</i>
